(Penske Automotive Group, Inc. \(NYSE: PAG\) faces structural vulnerability in its proposed take-private transaction by Motown Acquisition Corp. \(64% Penske) Tj
T* (Corporation, 36% Mitsui & Co.\). The transaction relies on a bifurcated stockholder approval structure where the Kahn v. M&F Worldwide Corp. \(MFW\) minority) Tj
T* (cleansing prong is contractually defined as 'a majority of the votes cast by the disinterested stockholders \(as defined in Section 144 of the DGCL\)' rather than a) Tj
T* (majority of all outstanding unaffiliated shares. This votes-cast formulation creates an identifiable litigation target under Delaware Chancery Court entire fairness) Tj
T* (jurisprudence, compounded by an 8.6% premium over the pre-announcement unaffected price \($212.00 cash vs. $210.00 initial bid, $195.21 unaffected) Tj
T* (baseline\). Concurrently, closing is conditioned on securing complex OEM change-of-control consents across global franchise networks and executing debt) Tj
T* (backstops for a $502.7M mandatory 101% par Change-of-Control Put on PAG's 3.75% Senior Subordinated Notes due 2029.) Tj
